---
name: Enable Node.js Debugger & Log Access for Debugging
description: This rule informs Cursor AI that it has access to advanced debugging capabilities    via a Node.js MCP debugger and direct log file tailing.   It should use these tools when debugging application issues.
alwaysApply: false
when: debugging application behavior, runtime errors, or unexpected logic flow
then: |
  You can use the following debugging resources:
  
  1. **Node.js Debugger (MCP Server)**  
     - Tool: `nodejs-debugger` MCP server  
     - Docs: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@hyperdrive-eng/mcp-nodejs-debugger  
     - Capabilities: Set breakpoints, step through code, inspect variables during runtime.

  2. **Real-time Application Logs**  
     You can access logs by tailing the following files (last 100 lines as an example):  
     - `logs/combined.log` — General combined logs  
     - `logs/error.log` — Error-specific logs  
     Example:  
     ```bash
     tail -n 100 logs/combined.log
     tail -n 100 logs/error.log
     ```

  Use the Node.js debugger for step-by-step code inspection and use logs for historical and contextual debugging.